# Baseline B-12 (F-17): PULL {n: 2} pages a 5-row result as 2, 2 and 1
# records; each page that leaves records ends with has_more: true and the
# last page with a SUCCESS. What this adds over
# boltkit/v4.0/return_5_records.bolt and readme_example.bolt (one n = 3
# page, then the rest): a smaller n, two has_more pages in a row, and a
# short last page. Only fields, the records per page and has_more are
# pinned; the page SUCCESS's t_last and db are not.
!: BOLT 4.4
!: AUTO HELLO
!: AUTO GOODBYE

C: RUN "UNWIND range(1, 5) AS i RETURN i" {} {}
   PULL {"n": 2}
S: SUCCESS {"fields": ["i"]}
   RECORD [1]
   RECORD [2]
   SUCCESS {"has_more": true}
C: PULL {"n": 2}
S: RECORD [3]
   RECORD [4]
   SUCCESS {"has_more": true}
C: PULL {"n": 2}
S: RECORD [5]
   SUCCESS {}
